/godotengine/godot/pulls/115926","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-02-09T11:31:58Z"},{"id":3775647905,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7hC9Ch","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"befea108bcaaf5eefabd6b9fb47f3dd56e112a67","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?u=c2e06a3d2b49a467aa907e54aa259516440267cc&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","login":"fire","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire"},"body":"This pull request is in the spirit of the constructive solid geometry design.\r\n\r\nI would not abbreviate `compat_mode` and instead write it as `compatibility_mode`.\r\n\r\nAlso we do not keep unused code in our codebase as a general rule.\r\n\r\nEdited:\r\n\r\nAs far as I know those are the changes requested, and I'll put an approve mark.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115926#pullrequestreview-3775647905","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115926","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-02-09T22:08:48Z"},{"id":3833540158,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7kfy4-","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"d5b8434c57c1a7cd53f42297d7300d41d9bc1001","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?u=c2e06a3d2b49a467aa907e54aa259516440267cc&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","login":"fire","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115926#pullrequestreview-3833540158","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115926","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-02-20T18:11:59Z"},{"id":3835918720,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7ko3mA","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?u=c2e06a3d2b49a467aa907e54aa259516440267cc&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","login":"fire","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire"},"body":"Asset pipeline Meeting:\n\n```\nbool uv_compatibility_mode = false;\n```\n\nSo enabling the new uv features should be set to true on the new projects and false on the old projects. Like default to true.\n\n@fire likes the fixes to the uv mapping.\n\nWaiting for the pr to be ready for review.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115926#pullrequestreview-3835918720","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115926","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-02-21T20:06:36Z"},{"id":3892865807,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7oCGsP","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"1cc88dff5a74116c4c33113c3f95385fa9cbd1e1","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n\r\nI think this has a lot of potential, but we need to make sure we get the UX on properties right (while keeping the compatibility constraints in mind). I'd appreciate more reviews from @godotengine/usability, as well as anyone versed in level design.\r\n\r\nIn the long term, we'll probably want some kind of higher-level editor for quick level design which uses CSG nodes as a backend, but exposes common actions through an overlay on the 3D editor viewport (e.g. create CSG nodes in a single click). In any case, we will need this feature to be available in CSG nodes so that future functionality can make use of it.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_pr_115926.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25753902/test_pr_115926.zip)\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1113\" height=\"981\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/40b92a18-0f6d-457e-a16f-48cf10a01369\" />\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- Top Material and Bottom Material should be in the Material section of the inspector. Right now, they are outside and therefore don't collapse if you collapse the Material section:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"288\" height=\"232\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f387a0ed-b5ad-46e0-bf31-16f418678ee2\" /> | <img width=\"288\" height=\"165\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a24b605a-afe4-45b9-83a3-b727d95a54da\" />\r\n-|-\r\n\r\n- Capitalization should be added to EditorPropertyNameProcessor for `uvs` -> `UVs`, below `uv2`: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/c53c5a1f49fa1edf97e6b570297c90a57d30a558/editor/inspector/editor_property_name_processor.cpp#L310\r\n\r\n- I think the Flip UVs property could do with more flexibility. Right now, textures like wooden planks may be misaligned, and you have to rotate the entire CSG node to fix this. This can be cumbersome if that CSG node has children, or an irregular shape where rotating it by 90° would lead to a different result than just rotating the UV.\r\n\r\n  - I suggest having one enum property to rotate the UV by 90-degree increments, and another enum property to flip the U axis, the V axis, or both. As I understand it, this computation should be trivial (unlike rotating by non-90 degree increments).\r\n\r\n- I'd like to see similar UV mapping options in CSGPolygon3D, so that the roof in the above example can have its tiles property scaled (they are way too large right now). I use a CSGPolygon3D for the roof as it's an easy way to create prism shapes.\r\n\r\n  - While in Depth mode, there could be separate Top and Bottom materials like in CSGBox3D.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115926#pullrequestreview-3892865807","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115926","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-03-05T00:38:15Z"},{"id":3909656577,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7pCKAB","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"90f57239dec522e3e7aabc7c4e064b141152e34d","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","login":"lyuma","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma"},"body":"We discussed this at the animation meeting. The uv flipping needs to be a separate change.\n\nI also think the code needed to support this and the uv flip is extremely complex and will make CSGBox3D and other shapes much more difficult to maintain.\n\nSpecial case for top and bottom material looks useful, but I just want to be able to see if it can be done without less complexity, and the UV flip code looks complicated. It would be nice if this could be done more generally somehow.\n\nThere was also an expressed opinion to have CSG use surface override.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115926#pullrequestreview-3909656577","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115926","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-03-07T21:07:40Z"}]